    "body": "Problem:\nAfter a buffer is changed while another window is current (e.g. nvim_buf_set_lines() from a float), undo moves the cursor to the other window's cursor position. Regression from 7e2e3f8c25: atom_origin_pos() falls back to curwin->w_cursor even if curwin shows a different buffer.\n\nTest name: it(\"u does not jump to other window's cursor position #42449\" ...",
